## 12) Agent — user action markers

When the reply needs **Andrew to do something manually** (edit a file on another machine, run a command, restart a service, etc.), wrap those instructions exactly like this:

```
######## DO THIS BEGIN ########
<steps Andrew must take>
####### END DO THIS #####
```

When the reply is **explanation only** and Andrew does **not** need to take any action, end the reply with:

```
>>>>> DO NOT DO, CURSOR JUST EXPLAIN <<<<<
```

Use **one** of these markers per reply (not both). Do not use them for steps Cursor already completed itself.

Ubuntu-only Postgres steps (see section 2, schema parity) use their own marker, **`######## DO THIS ON UBUNTU BEGIN ########` … `####### END DO THIS ON UBUNTU #####`**, which may appear alongside the markers above.
